    :note "first real end-to-end proof of the ADR's core ask (datomic/datascript-queryable compliance facts across repos); next tick proceeds to municipality Wave 0"}
   {:addendum 2
    :date "2026-07-14"
    :title "loop tick 2: municipality Wave 0 (Tokyo) landed, real data bug found+fixed, query-engine cardinality-many bug found+fixed"
    :artifacts {:municipality-repo "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-municipality-jpn-tokyo (new, initial commit) -- src/ordinance/facts.cljc (2 real reiki.metro.tokyo.lg.jp-cited Tokyo ordinances, WebFetch-verified title/number/date), schema/ordinance.edn, data/datascript-tx.edn, test/ordinance/facts_test.clj (4 tests/11 assertions green)"
                :data-bug-found-and-fixed "cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn/organization.edn :hq sourced Q262438 (Shigaraki Palace, Japan's 742-745AD capital) instead of Tokyo (Q1490) via com-etzhayyim-ooyake's gov-units.capitals.edn -- a Wikidata P36 multi-claim ingestion bug in ooyake itself (R1/verified-tier dataset). Fixed in this repo only (commit 15252d7); ooyake root cause NOT fixed, unclear if Japan-specific or systemic across its other 189 countries -- flagged as a follow-up outside this ADR's scope"
                :query-script-bug-found-and-fixed "compliance-fact-query.cljs's naive clj->js schema conversion silently broke :db.cardinality/many (array values stored as one opaque datom, not exploded) -- npm datascript's JS wrapper requires schema VALUE-side keywords as colon-prefixed strings (\":db.cardinality/many\"), unlike bare-string entity attrs/schema keys. Fixed via schema->js/schema-entry->js/->ds-schema-value; verified topic-based queries now return correct cross-repo results"
                :verified-run "3 repos (cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn / etzhayyim/global-legislation-datoms / cloud-itonami-municipality-jpn-tokyo), 572 facts unioned in one DataScript db, cardinality-many `topic` queries now correctly cross-match JPN statutes and Tokyo ordinances"}
    :note "next tick proceeds to remaining Wave 0 municipalities (USA/Washington D.C., GBR/London, ...)"}
   {:addendum 3
    :date "2026-07-14"
